; A mediator of pure SYMBOLS judges deterministically — no model fires for it.
;
; The mediator's tokens must appear in the ANSWERS, directly or one
; co-occurrence hop away: resolve_mediation scores each answer by round-trip
; holonomy against the mediator's own words, through a record built from the
; answers themselves. A mediator sharing no vocabulary with them scores every
; answer 1.0, refuses all of them, and the square yields nothing — which is
; correct behaviour and a useless test. Hence branches that answer in
; sentences, both containing the word the mediator judges on.
; expect: calls 2
; expect: clean
; expect: answers
([failure]
  "Answer with exactly: the failure is reproducible on every run"
  "Answer with exactly: the failure appears at random")
